WEBVTT

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:19.330
A light so bright that it can't be hidden
Breaks the silence and resurrects in this world

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:30.040
The dry land quakes violently
Sparks clash as we risk our lives

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:37.810
Let a miracle occur, just one more time

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:44.950
The power to regain the pages of memories I lost long ago

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:53.050
The trusting heart pierces the darkness
Search for the place where the soul rests

00:00:53.180 --> 00:00:59.200
The sharp glint in my unblinking eye burns

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:06.700
Two souls - light and shadow
To the future shown in the crystal

00:01:06.930 --> 00:01:13.310
Now moving  Overflowing in red  eyes

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:23.000
The Story That Ends In Light

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.220
Partner, this is my final ace in the hole.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:28.940
My most powerful servant, Dark Magician!

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:33.750
I forgot Atem still had Dark Magician in his deck.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.070
Dark Magician...

00:01:36.070 --> 00:01:41.800
It's a great ally, but the most dangerous foe.

00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:45.180
But if I don't destroy it, I can't win!

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.730
My turn!  I draw!

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:52.480
I summon a monster in defense position!

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:57.790
Due to the Equip Spell, Dark Magician has 2800 attack points.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:00.660
I don’t have a monster right now that can destroy it.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.510
I switch Curse of Dragon to defense position.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:06.260
I end my turn.

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:09.780
All he can do is strengthen his defenses.

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.210
Not necessarily.

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:17.890
That set monster in defense position should be trouble for Atem.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:21.220
The monster that Yugi set...

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:28.730
Due to Witch of the Black Forest, I get a monster with 1500 or lower defense points from my deck.

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.920
I add Marshmallon to my hand!

00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:33.660
That card must be Marshmallon.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:36.620
When it's attacked while it's set in defense position...

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.590
...it deals 1000 points of damage to the opponent.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:43.060
That monster also can't be destroyed in battle.

00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:45.430
I have 700 life points left.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:48.230
If I attack carelessly, I'll lose.

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:52.530
Partner, that strategy won’t work on me!

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:55.330
My turn!  I draw!

00:02:55.330 --> 00:02:58.420
The spell card, Thousand Knives!

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:04.800
The Pharaoh is still drawing the right cards at the right time.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.740
The Pharaoh is a dueling god.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:14.410
When Dark Magician is on my field, Thousand Knives destroys one of your monsters!

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:16.610
Go, Dark Magician!

00:03:21.380 --> 00:03:22.690
Marshmallon!

00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:27.580
When Marshmallon is destroyed in facedown defense position, its effect doesn’t activate!

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:32.250
Dark Magician, attack Curse of Dragon!

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.250
Black Magic!

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:40.840
Yugi!

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:45.250
Jonouchi!  Instead of having the advantage, Yugi's monsters are all destroyed!

00:03:45.250 --> 00:03:47.520
Give it your all, Yugi!

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:48.620
Big brother!

00:03:48.620 --> 00:03:51.640
He changed the tide of battle in an instant.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.280
Dark Magician is dangerous!

00:03:54.280 --> 00:03:58.710
Atem and Dark Magician truly are strong.

00:03:58.710 --> 00:04:02.670
Is there a weakness in their powerful bond?

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:05.180
Partner, it’s your turn.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:08.190
My turn!  I draw!

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:13.190
I summon Blockman from my hand in defense position!

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:19.360
Then I set one card and end my turn.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:20.200
Here I go!

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:22.200
It’s my turn!  I draw!

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:26.710
I equip my spell card, Dark Spear on Dark Magician!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:33.080
When Dark Spear is equipped on Dark Magician...

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:36.850
...if it has more attack points than your monster’s defense points...

00:04:36.850 --> 00:04:40.090
...it deals you the difference as damage!

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.090
Here I go, partner!

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:46.090
Dark Magician, attack Blockman!

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:51.500
I activate my trap, Soul Shield!

00:04:55.260 --> 00:05:03.200
By paying half my life points, Soul Shield negates the battle and ends your Battle Phase!

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.830
Dark Magician’s attack didn't reach me!

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:09.370
I end my turn.

00:05:10.330 --> 00:05:12.330
He managed to survive.

00:05:12.330 --> 00:05:15.720
But Yugi only has 400 life points left.

00:05:15.720 --> 00:05:19.030
Atem only has 700 life points too.

00:05:19.030 --> 00:05:23.370
If either's attack succeeds, this duel could be over.

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:31.380
I told Anzu that she had to watch the duel, but even I don’t feel like watching.

00:05:31.380 --> 00:05:36.540
Yugi and Atem... It's rough that you have to fight each other.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:38.010
My turn!

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:40.910
He’s planning something.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.010
I draw!

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.380
I have to take a risk.

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:51.390
I activate the spell card, Gold Sarcophagus from my hand!

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.430
Gold Sarcophagus?

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:59.370
I select a card from my deck or hand and place it inside Gold Sarcophagus.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:02.810
If you play the same card, its effect is negated.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.420
What card did he put inside?

00:06:13.420 --> 00:06:14.800
That box...

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:18.550
It's the same box where he kept the Millennium Puzzle.

00:06:18.550 --> 00:06:21.620
The box that contained the Millennium Puzzle...

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:25.490
That's how Yugi met the other Yugi.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:27.430
It's the box of friendship.

00:06:27.430 --> 00:06:31.440
I activate Blockman’s effect!

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:32.990
Block Separation!

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:40.760
Blockman counts as a tribute for every turn that passed since it was summoned.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.450
So Blockman counts as two tributes.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:46.280
I tribute the two Blockmans!

00:06:46.280 --> 00:06:50.220
I’ll use this monster to destroy Dark Magician!

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.460
Come forth!

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.310
Gandora the Dragon of Destruction!

00:06:58.310 --> 00:06:59.310
That’s...

00:06:59.710 --> 00:07:01.770
Gandora the Dragon of Destruction!

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.770
Gandora...

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:09.550
That’s the monster Yugi used to defeat Yami Bakura in the world of memories.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:15.670
And signified that Yugi will part ways with the other Yugi.

00:07:19.300 --> 00:07:24.490
Gandora can only remain on the field on the turn it's summoned.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:32.660
But by paying half my life points, it removes all monsters on the field from play!

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:35.220
I activate Gandora’s effect!

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:37.220
Destroy Gigarays!

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:43.440
I flip over my trap card, Dark Illusion!

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:59.070
When the trap card Dark Illusion activates, it protects Dark Magician from effects that turn!

00:07:59.070 --> 00:08:03.480
No way...  Even Gandora couldn’t defeat Dark Magician...

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:09.480
But due to this card’s effect, you can draw one card from your deck.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.710
Partner, draw a card.

00:08:14.230 --> 00:08:16.820
I set two cards.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:18.270
I end my turn.

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:22.710
Yugi has no monsters again.

00:08:22.710 --> 00:08:24.710
This is bad, big brother!

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.710
Yugi's going to lose for sure!

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:31.950
Yugi is just a vessel after all.  He can't defeat the Pharaoh.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.050
Yugi...

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:41.730
No, Yugi hasn't lost his fighting spirit yet.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:44.170
My turn!  I draw!

00:08:44.170 --> 00:08:47.700
Dark Magician attacks you directly!

00:08:49.370 --> 00:08:51.150
I activate my trap card!

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:52.640
Magician's Circle!

00:08:53.580 --> 00:08:58.200
When your Spellcaster-Type monster attacks me...

00:08:58.200 --> 00:09:02.530
...I can Special Summon a Spellcaster from my deck!

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:05.570
That’s an anti-Dark Magician card.

00:09:05.570 --> 00:09:09.970
As I expected, Yugi was prepared to counter Dark Magician.

00:09:09.970 --> 00:09:14.340
I Special Summon Silent Magician from my deck!

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:21.600
But Magician's Circle’s effect also works on my deck!

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:26.390
Emerge from my deck, Dark Magician Girl!

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:30.310
Dark Magician Girl!

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.990
Let’s continue the battle, partner!

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:36.170
Dark Magician!

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.620
Attack Silent Magician!

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:43.470
Yugi’s monster only has 1000 attack points!

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.410
If he takes this attack...

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.740
It's not over yet, my other self!

00:10:11.740 --> 00:10:14.940
I promised to defeat you in this duel!

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:17.300
I activate my spell card!

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:19.390
Spell Textbook!

00:10:22.300 --> 00:10:26.880
By discarding every card in my hand, I can draw one card from my deck.

00:10:26.880 --> 00:10:30.270
If that card is a spell, I can activate it immediately!

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:32.710
I have zero cards in my hand!

00:10:32.710 --> 00:10:34.640
So I don’t have to discard any cards!

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:40.080
This will be the final draw that will determine our destiny!

00:10:43.320 --> 00:10:46.890
I activate the spell card, Card of Sanctity!

00:10:46.890 --> 00:10:51.290
We both draw until we each have 6 cards in our hands!

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:58.160
Silent Magician’s effect activates!

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:04.340
For every card you draw, Silent Magician gains 500 attack points!

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:07.270
I drew 5 cards!

00:11:07.270 --> 00:11:12.910
Silent Magician rises to Level 5 and 3500 attack points!

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:17.360
Resume Dark Magician’s attack!

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.150
Atem has 700 life points.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:24.360
If this Battle Phase occurs, Yugi wins!

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:32.750
I activate a Quick-Play Spell from my hand!

00:11:33.650 --> 00:11:35.670
Magicians Unite!

00:11:35.670 --> 00:11:40.010
If I have at least two Spellcasters on my field...

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:45.040
...I can treat the two as one monster with 3000 attack points!

00:12:10.290 --> 00:12:12.140
Impressive, partner.

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:15.210
You defeated my ace, Dark Magician.

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:18.420
We both only have 200 life points.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:19.880
Our backs are to the wall.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:22.820
The time has come to end this.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:41.120
You used Card of Sanctity to turn this duel around, but it now allows me to turn the tables.

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:45.170
It gave me the card to end this duel.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:47.870
From my hand...

00:12:48.450 --> 00:12:52.080
I activate the spell card, Monster Reborn!

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:58.320
Resurrect, Slifer the Sky Dragon!

00:13:03.660 --> 00:13:04.690
What?

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:07.090
Slifer shows up now?

00:13:07.090 --> 00:13:11.650
Slifer’s attack points are determined by the number of cards in my hand.

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:13.470
I have four cards in my hand.

00:13:13.470 --> 00:13:16.940
Therefore, Slifer has 4000 attack points!

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:20.910
Partner, I win.

00:13:25.140 --> 00:13:28.490
I knew you were going to do that, my other self.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:32.490
Because if I were you, I'd summon a God too.

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:35.650
That’s...

00:13:38.820 --> 00:13:42.760
I remove Gold Sarcophagus's seal!

00:13:50.510 --> 00:13:53.310
The card he put inside is coming out!

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:02.110
Monster Reborn!

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:08.080
Since I put Monster Reborn inside Gold Sarcophagus, you can't play it.

00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:13.450
So Special Summoning Slifer is negated.

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:20.630
Slifer is disappearing.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:25.200
Monster Reborn would've been useful for Yugi.

00:14:25.200 --> 00:14:27.800
But he chose to seal it away instead.

00:14:27.800 --> 00:14:32.580
Yugi is sending Atem a message.

00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:36.590
The soul of the dead must not remain in the world of the living.

00:14:36.590 --> 00:14:40.590
It’s a requiem for the Pharaoh’s soul to travel to the afterlife.

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:44.160
It symbolizes that Yugi has decided to part with him.

00:14:44.800 --> 00:14:47.770
Yugi figured out my card.

00:14:49.090 --> 00:14:51.590
He has surpassed me.

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:01.570
Atem has no monsters to defend with.

00:15:01.580 --> 00:15:05.410
If Silent Magician attacks him directly, the duel is over.

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:06.950
Yugi...

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:13.030
Do it, partner!

00:15:14.180 --> 00:15:18.920
Silent Magician attacks you directly!

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.200
I lose, Yugi.

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:07.570
Stand up.  The winner isn’t supposed to be down on his knees.

00:16:07.570 --> 00:16:10.990
If I were you, I wouldn’t cry.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:18.240
Since I’m such a weakling, you were always someone I wanted to live up to.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.520
I wanted to be strong like you.

00:16:22.000 --> 00:16:24.660
You’re not a weakling.

00:16:24.660 --> 00:16:28.240
You always had a strength that was unmatched by anyone.

00:16:28.240 --> 00:16:30.240
A strength called kindness.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:33.670
That's what I learned from you...

00:16:33.670 --> 00:16:34.670
...partner.

00:16:36.340 --> 00:16:43.380
Your courage to accept this battle ritual showed me the road I must travel.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:45.230
My other self...

00:16:45.230 --> 00:16:48.690
I am no longer another you.

00:16:49.420 --> 00:16:52.510
You are you - and no one else.

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:57.040
You are the only Yugi Muto in the world!

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:03.370
What’s going on?

00:17:03.370 --> 00:17:04.700
The eye on the door!

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:09.110
Due to the battle ritual, the Eye of Udjat that guards the door...

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:12.320
... has determined the Pharaoh’s soul is real.

00:17:12.320 --> 00:17:19.720
After wandering this world for 3,000 years, the Pharaoh's soul can now move on.

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:28.170
Soul of the Pharaoh, say the Pharaoh's name to the Eye of Udjat!

00:17:32.210 --> 00:17:34.570
My name is Atem!

00:17:47.280 --> 00:17:48.570
Yugi!

00:17:49.750 --> 00:17:51.440
Wait, Yugi!

00:17:51.440 --> 00:17:53.250
You're really leaving?

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:57.760
You don’t have to go to the afterlife!

00:17:57.760 --> 00:17:59.350
Don't go!

00:18:02.580 --> 00:18:04.580
The other Yugi-

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:07.290
No, I mean Atem.

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:13.070
I understand that your home is on the other side of that light.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:14.990
I do understand.

00:18:14.990 --> 00:18:21.780
But for us, that light symbolizes the border that will separate us!

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:24.780
That's what I don't understand!

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:30.240
After all this time together, our friend is going to vanish right before our eyes!

00:18:30.240 --> 00:18:32.000
I don’t understand why!

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:35.790
Anzu, you don’t have to understand.

00:18:36.800 --> 00:18:41.330
Since we can’t understand, we have to burn him into our memories!

00:18:41.330 --> 00:18:47.270
So that we'll never forget the time we spent with him!

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:50.810
So let’s send him on his way.

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:53.140
To his future!

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:55.070
Everyone...

00:18:55.070 --> 00:18:59.010
I'll never forget you.

00:18:59.010 --> 00:19:00.820
Yugi!

00:19:00.820 --> 00:19:04.120
You may call yourself Pharaoh or Atem, you’re always Yugi to me!

00:19:04.120 --> 00:19:07.830
Even if a thousand years pass, you’re still our friend!

00:19:08.640 --> 00:19:09.490
Right!

00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:12.430
I’ll never forget you!

00:19:45.370 --> 00:19:46.620
Yugi!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.160
My other self...

00:19:56.260 --> 00:19:57.300
What?

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:58.240
An earthquake?

00:19:59.880 --> 00:20:01.970
The Tablet of the Afterlife!

00:20:04.150 --> 00:20:05.760
The Millennium Items!

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:07.350
Yugi, let’s go!

00:20:07.350 --> 00:20:09.450
It’s too dangerous here!

00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:11.540
Everyone, we have to get out!

00:20:15.280 --> 00:20:16.310
Hurry!

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:40.260
The Pharaoh’s soul has moved on, so the Millennium Items have fulfilled their duties.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:43.720
The Door to the Afterlife will never open again.

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:46.460
He really left.

00:20:46.930 --> 00:20:47.930
Yeah.

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:25.280
Right now, we don't need a map

00:21:25.440 --> 00:21:41.000
The miracle that tore through the darkness is in my hand

00:21:41.720 --> 00:21:46.840
Without a goal in mind

00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:55.410
We just step towards our dream

00:21:55.800 --> 00:22:01.050
EYE'S  As you sense it

00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:09.520
Your eye will find it

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:15.330
Oh! EYE'S  What you wish for

00:22:16.120 --> 00:22:23.470
Will touch your soul

00:22:23.660 --> 00:22:26.730
In a duel

00:22:40.280 --> 00:22:42.390
Grandpa, I’m off!

00:22:42.390 --> 00:22:44.450
Be careful.

00:22:44.450 --> 00:22:46.430
Yugi, good morning!

00:22:46.430 --> 00:22:47.120
Hey!

00:22:47.120 --> 00:22:49.340
Good morning, everyone!

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:51.220
You’re late, Yugi!

00:22:49.340 --> 00:22:53.290
This wasn’t a story unique to the Pharaoh.

00:22:51.220 --> 00:22:52.400
Sorry.

00:22:53.290 --> 00:23:00.520
Every person has a story, and the story ends in light.

00:22:53.450 --> 00:22:56.060
I bet you pulled an all-nighter building your deck!

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:06.340
And my story has only begun.
